 (dispersion 4%), and the Monte Carlo range runs $214 to $493 (P10-P90).","On multiples it looks cheap against Healthcare peers: P/E 8.1 vs 26.2, EV/EBITDA 6.5 vs 15.5 and P/FCF 13.2 vs 23.8 (sector median).","The EBIT multiple is close to its own 10-year median (-5%).","Earnings yields are attractive: an FCF yield of 7.6% (above the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 11.5% (vs the 8% bar).","The 17 covering analysts target $195 on average, 1% above the price, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 11% earns above the cost of capital of 8.0%, but the 3pp spread is short of the 7pp moat bar; returns have been steady (CV 0.18).","It converts 5% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality looks solid: cash conversion of 1.25x.","ROE of 20% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (2.1x equity multiplier).","It spends 0.6% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is moderate at 1.8x net debt to EBITDA ($137.8M of cash against $4.8B of debt), above the 1.5x gate, with interest covered 12.8x."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 9.0% over 3 years, 8.5% over 5 years and 5.9% over 10 years.","Net reinvestment is nil (capex and working capital no more than cover depreciation), so fundamental growth is near zero.","Free cash flow has compounded -12.2% a year over five years, short of the 5% durability bar.","Capex runs 1.6x depreciation (5.8% of sales), so it is building capacity for future growth.","Its Rule of 40 score is 13, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business.","Analysts expect 2.1% long-term annual earnings growth."],"own":["Insiders own 5.1%, meaningful skin in the game, and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","It returns 9.0% a year to shareholders (8.5% in buybacks and 0.4% in dividends).","The share count has shrunk 5.7% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake.","It has paid a dividend for 23 consecutive years, raising it 24.2% a year over the last five."],"people":["With about 102,000 employees, each generates about $170K of revenue, 0.5x the Healthcare median, and revenue has grown 7.9% a year across its filed history.","That works out to $8K of free cash flow per employee.","The company is founder-led, which often keeps management aligned with long-term owners.","CEO pay is $6.1M (36x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores poorly (8/10, lower is better)."]},"profile":{"v":"INVEST","conv":76,"head":"Invest: trades 41% below fair value of $327; revenue grew 8.5%/yr over 5y.","pros":["Composite 55, above the 39 line (gates 17/25)","Trades 41% below fair value of $327","Revenue grew 8.5%/yr over 5y","Altman Z in the safe zone","P/E 8.1x vs sector 26.2x"],"cons":["12-1 month momentum -21%"],"flags":[],"need":[],"buy_below":278.34,"vc":{"base":327.45,"base_src":"dcf","bear":213.59,"bull":492.82,"alt_median":322.18,"n_alt":3,"gap":0.0164,"dispersion":0.0418,"level":"MEDIUM","why":[]},"med":{"pe":26.2222,"ev_ebitda":15.54,"pfcf":23.7593,"pb":3.4965,"roic":-0.1287,"gross_margin":0.5566,"fcf_margin":0.0222,"div_yield":0.0136}},"mc_quantiles":[144.76,187.76,213.59,235.48,251.37,266.84,279.05,292.01,306.44,319.33,333.51,345.24,358.67,372.87,392.38,411.78,436.94,463.11,492.82,542.88,690.46],"mc_drivers":{"growth":0.543,"discount_rate":0.209,"terminal_growth":0.02,"exit_multiple":0.228},"ticker":"UHS","date":"2026-11-13"}